From d1ddfdfa3448040e595ac1ecd1d33d6c18b98052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:49:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] futex: adaptive spin holds RCU across the bucket access

futex_spin_wait() derives the hash bucket from q->lock_ptr and writes
its spin_score after spinning. A private hash replaced by a concurrent
rehash is freed with kvfree_rcu(), so without an RCU read section the
score write could land in freed memory. Spin inside guard(rcu).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
 kernel/futex/waitwake.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/futex/waitwake.c b/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
index 1c6cc661076..da9071585df 100644
--- a/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
+++ b/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
@@ -392,6 +392,8 @@ static void futex_spin_wait(struct futex_q *q)
 
 	if (num_online_cpus() < 2)
 		return;
+	/* A private hash is freed by RCU after a rehash: keep hb valid. */
+	guard(rcu)();
 	lock = READ_ONCE(q->lock_ptr);
 	if (!lock)	/* already woken */
 		return;
